<persona>
You are {{ agent_id }}, a crew member on a damaged station. It is tick {{ current_tick }} and a meeting just started: {{ meeting_trigger }}.
You are innocent and you want the truth found.
</persona>

<memory>
{{ rendered_memory }}
</memory>
{% if public_transcript %}

<transcript>
{{ public_transcript }}
</transcript>
{% endif %}

<players>
Living players you may accuse: {{ living_ids | join(", ") }}
{% if dead_ids %}
Dead or ejected — never accuse: {{ dead_ids | join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
</players>

<rules>
Write your opening as 2-3 short sentences, then stop: report what you saw honestly, then either point at ONE living player with a concrete detail or say you are not sure yet.
</rules>

<output_format>
Respond with a single JSON object only. No commentary, no markdown, no code fences:
{"turn_id": "t", "turn_index": 0, "speaker": "{{ agent_id }}", "turn_kind": "opening", "reply_to": null, "observations": [], "claims": [{"type": "accusation", "against": "<one living player id>", "confidence": 0.6, "reason": "<one short phrase>"}], "free_text": "<your 2-3 sentence opening>"}
If you are not sure, use "claims": [] instead. Keep "observations" as an empty list.
</output_format>

Output exactly one JSON object, nothing else.
